## V1 (position straight from Servo) vs V2 (trajectory output): single moves

Single step-and-hold moves make the position-shift estimator ill-posed (flat cost while the arm holds), so these use the velocity cross-correlation lag, and only the component the move exercises: translation for the 10 cm moves, rotation for the 90° moves, both for general motion. Search limit 1.6 s.

| Run | mode | component | lag (ms) |
|---|---|---|---|
| V1/V1_90_Degrees_Forwards | position_v1 | rotation | 1604 (≥ search limit) |
| V1/V1_90_Degrees_Left | position_v1 | rotation | 1604 (≥ search limit) |
| V1/V1_90_Degrees_Twist | position_v1 | rotation | 1604 (≥ search limit) |
| V1/V1_Forwards_10CM | position_v1 | translation | 433 |
| V1/V1_Sideways_10CM | position_v1 | translation | 505 |
| V1/V1_Vertical_10CM | position_v1 | translation | 377 |
| V2/General_Motion_Fast | trajectory | both | 140 / 254 |
| V2/General_Motion_Slow | trajectory | both | 159 / 133 |
| V2/IN_10CM | trajectory | translation | 132 |
